  "question_stem": "A train travels between two stations, $A$ and $B$. The train starts from rest at $A$ and accelerates at a constant rate for $T$ s until it reaches a speed of $25 \\text{ m s}^{-1}$. It then travels at this constant speed before decelerating at a constant rate, coming to rest at $B$. The magnitude of the train's deceleration is twice the magnitude of its acceleration. The total time taken for the journey is $180$ s.",
  "context_texts": [
    "A trapezium-shaped velocity-time graph rising linearly from 0 to 25, remaining at 25, then falling linearly to 0 with the right-hand slope twice as steep as the left-hand slope.",
    "$180-1.5T$ seconds."
  ],
